      "title": "Amazon EBS",
      "items": [
        "Block storage pinned to one Availability Zone and attached to a single node",
        "With gp3 you set IOPS and throughput independently of volume size",
        "Suits latency-sensitive single-writer workloads such as databases"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Amazon EFS",
      "items": [
        "A regional NFS file system that many pods across AZs write to at once",
        "Fits shared content, log collection, and user uploads that need RWX",
        "Elastic throughput mode scales throughput automatically with the workload"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "FSx for Lustre",
      "items": [
        "A high-performance parallel file system reaching hundreds of GB/s",
        "Linking it to S3 as a data repository suits training datasets",
        "Used for HPC simulation and large-scale machine learning training"
      ]
